=== PARITY (vs web DoorWindowStatusWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (DoorWindowSource -> DoorWindowModel):
    useVehicles (default vehicle id), useSecurityLatest(id, 5s), useTranslation. The production app
    wires DoorWindowSource over the shared security state holder; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> a 1:1 port of the web helpers, executed-green by XCTest:
    • parseWindowState: boolean -> open/closed; asNonEmptyString gate (length>0, NO trim);
      "closed" -> closed; contains "vent"/"partial" -> partial; else -> open.
    • parseDoorStates: boolean -> all open/closed; "all_closed"/"allclosed" -> all closed; non-empty CSV
      seeds all-closed then applies per-token open rules (driver/passenger × front/rear, front/rear ×
      left/right, bare "open" -> all). Per-token trim+lowercase + filter Boolean; web else-if precedence
      preserved (exactly one rule fires per token).
    • toGridStatus: closed->ok, open/partial->warning, unknown->unknown. toValueLabel: Closed/Open/
      Partial/em-dash. openDoorCount = doors === open; openWindowCount = windows !== closed && !== unknown.
    • 4 door + 4 window StatusCells (ids door-fl..rr / window-fl..rr) ALWAYS produced; compact summaries
      "Doors ✓" / "N door(s) open" + "Windows ✓" / "N window(s) open".
  Composition -> shell chrome (door icon + "Door & Window Status" title [hidden when 1x1] + freshness
    chip + refresh) · 1x1 CompactView (doors + windows summary chips, web CompactView) · standard/tall
    (Doors section + Windows section, each a 2-col status grid; inter-section spacing widens when
    rows>=2, web isTall space-y-4 vs space-y-2) · empty grid ("No door/window data", web
    WidgetStatusGrid empty branch).
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone (compiled against the
    REAL apps/apple Tokens + Components/UI/Badges in the iOS+macOS typechecks below). DoorWindowChip
    mirrors the TSBadge tokens, extended to take a pre-localized String (our per-surface table).
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No door/window data") · error (retry
    affordance) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content. Model phase
    resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell (skeleton only
    on initial fetch; empty grid only when securityData is absent).
  i18n -> all 15 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.doorWindow.{title,doors,windows,closed,open,partial,fl,fr,rl,rr,doorsAllClosed,doorsOpen,
    windowsAllClosed,windowsOpen,noData} -> ALL PRESENT in DoorWindowStatusWidget.strings, plus the
    registry description + native chrome keys. No English literals in native code (verbatim facade).
  a11y -> each status tile carries a combined "<position>, <value>" label; section headers tagged
    isHeader; compact row a combined door+window summary; refresh button an accessibilityLabel; freshness
